url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2724,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","hacktoberfest","java","kubernetes","reactive"],"visibility":"public","forks":3033,"open_issues":2724,"watchers":15335,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nWhen using Qute 2.16.12 I am trying to call a CDI bean's method with the signature \r\n`public String executeFunction(Invocable invocable, String functionName, Object... args)`.\r\nCalling this function without any arguments works fine, however, providing one or more arguments (myProperty is a string in this case) results in\r\n`Rendering error: Method \"executeFunction(jsExecutionContext,\"jsFunctionName\",myProperty.or(null))\" not found on the base object \"*packages*.FunctionTemplateExtension_Subclass\" in expression {cdi:functionTemplateExtension.executeFunction(jsExecutionContext,\"jsFunctionName\",myProperty.or(null))}`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe method is called correctly and the resulting string is rendered.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe method is not called and a TemplateException with the message:\r\n`Rendering error: Method \"executeFunction(jsExecutionContext,\"jsFunctionName\",myProperty.or(null))\" not found on the base object \"*packages*.FunctionTemplateExtension_Subclass\" in expression {cdi:functionTemplateExtension.executeFunction(jsExecutionContext,\"jsFunctionName\",myProperty.or(null))}`\r\nis thrown.\n\n### How to Reproduce?\n\nRender a Qute template in Qute 2.16.12 with the string\r\n`{cdi:functionTemplateExtension.executeFunction(jsExecutionContext,\"coalesce\",param1,param2)}`\r\non an extension (marked as `@Dependent @Named(\"functionTemplateExtension\")`) with a method `public String executeFunction(Invocable invocable, String functionName, Object... args)`  \n\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\n\nLinux Hostname 5.15.146.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2 #1 SMP Thu Jan 11 04:09:03 UTC 2024 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\n\n### Output of `java -version`\n\n openjdk version \"17.0.9\" 2023-10-17 LTS OpenJDK Runtime Environment Corretto-17.0.9.8.1 (build 17.0.9+8-LTS) OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM Corretto-17.0.9.8.1 (build 17.0.9+8-LTS, mixed mode, sharing)\n\n### Quarkus version or git rev\n\n2.16.12.Final\n\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\n\nApache Maven 3.6.3 (Red Hat 3.6.3-13)\n\n### Additional information\n\nI've seen other reports mentioning errors with 1 varargs parameter ( e.g. https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/31449 ), but they don't seem connected as my version should contain the fix and the errors still occur when having two or more parameters.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/40072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/40072/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]